      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Osteoid osteoma is a small, benign, and painful tumor most commonly affecting the extra-articular portions of the long bones, especially the femur or tibia. Osteoid osteoma of the coracoid process is so rare that we have found only three previously reported cases in the international literature. We describe our experience in managing a case of osteoid osteoma in this unusual location."},
